From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Sun, 24 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: program the best N-PHY RSSI VCM instead of the loop bound

b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_cal() sweeps the eight narrowband RSSI VCM settings of a
core, polls each one, and picks the one whose I and Q results are closest to
zero into vcm_final. It then programs the winner back into the radio - and
on N-PHY rev 7 and up it programs vcm instead, which is the sweep's loop
variable and is 8 by the time the loop has ended.

Eight is not a VCM. The field is three bits wide, so on radio 2057 the
maskset writes bit 3 of NB_MASTER, which is outside the field, and leaves
the VCM field at whatever the last sweep iteration put there. The result of
the search is discarded on every rev 7 and up, and a bit that belongs to
something else gets set.

The rev 3 branch immediately below has it right, and so does the reference:
wlc_phy_rssi_cal_nphy_rev3() passes vcm_final on both paths.

Measured on an MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362, N-PHY rev 8 with
radio 2057 rev 8: with the fix the port writes the VCM the vendor driver
writes on the second core, 3 on both sides, where before it wrote 8.

Not tested on hardware.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n22498
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/HEAD/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded

Records #22377 to #23541 of that capture are the two VCM sweeps of the
second RSSI calibration, one per core. The write that selects the winner for
core 1 is

  53677.056000 #23537    cpu0 RAD.MOD  addr=0x0139 val=0x0003 mask=0x0007

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -2183,7 +2183,7 @@ static void b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_cal(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 			b43_radio_maskset(dev,
 					  core ? R2057_NB_MASTER_CORE1 :
 						 R2057_NB_MASTER_CORE0,
-					  ~R2057_VCM_MASK, vcm);
+					  ~R2057_VCM_MASK, vcm_final);
 		else
 			b43_radio_maskset(dev, r | B2056_RX_RSSI_MISC,
 					  0xE3, vcm_final << 2);
